From: Knockout Kernels <build@localhost>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gki_defconfig: strip debug/instrumentation/kunit-test
 configs for performance builds

Disables kernel-side debug and test instrumentation that has a real
runtime cost on a production device: KASAN, UBSAN, KFENCE, page
owner/pinner tracking, memory-init poisoning, schedstats, ftrace hist
triggers, PM debug hooks, CMA debugfs stats, CONTEXTIDR PID tracing,
softlockup/workqueue watchdogs, and the KUNIT test modules scattered
through the tree (they build as modules and don't autoload, but this
keeps them out of the module list entirely).

Left untouched on purpose:
  - CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF / DWARF5 / compressed — build-time only,
    zero runtime cost, and build_kernel() in build.sh checks for BTF
    being enabled and warns if pahole can't produce it.
  - CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS, TASKSTATS/TASK_*ACCT — required by
    vendor modules and Android battery/procstats respectively; not
    "debug" in the perf sense.

Since ABI/KMI protected-exports enforcement is already stripped by
main() in build.sh (rm abi_gki_protected_exports_*, protected_modules
= [] in modules.bzl) before this patch is applied, none of these
changes need to preserve KMI symbol stability — this tree is not
meant to interoperate with a stock GKI boot image.
